// Fixture for the `oskel build` extern-error test (tests/build_error.cmake).
//
// `getpid` is a real C symbol the development VM resolves through its host
// registry, so this program runs on the VM. The AOT backend has no host to
// resolve an `extern "C"` symbol against (the FFI lowering is PHASE 7f), so
// `oskel build` must fail with the dedicated message instead of the generic
// unassigned-global one a typo produces.
extern "C" {
  fn getpid(): int;
}
print(getpid());
